.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
data/
*.csv
!tests/fixtures/*.csv
*.parquet

# ...EXCEPT the replay bundles. They are the one Parquet in this repository
# that is meant to be published: a few hundred kilobytes per run that let a
# reader recompute every budget metric without the dataset. The blanket rule
# above silently dropped them -- `bundle.json` committed, the data files not --
# so the archive looked complete and the verification test passed locally and
# failed in a clean clone. Same shape as the bare `gold/` rule that once
# matched at any depth.
!results_archive/replay/**/*.parquet

# Pipeline stage outputs: tens of GB of Parquet, regenerable from the raw
# input. Anchored to data/ on purpose -- a bare `gold/` matches ANY directory
# of that name at ANY depth, and it silently swallowed results_archive/gold/,
# which is how every published figure ended up with no artifact behind it in
# CI. The manifests there are the provenance for the README; they must ship.
data/bronze/
data/silver/
data/gold/

# The manifests behind every published number. 3.6 MB of JSON, no Parquet.
# Committed so that `scripts/make_tables.py --check` can verify the documents
# in CI and so a reader who clones this can verify them too.
!results_archive/
!results_archive/**/*.json
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
